{"criterion":"blast-radius","verdicts":[{"finding_id":"standalone-review:code-reviewer-1","verdict":"upheld","reasoning":"The mis-set flag genuinely reaches consumers: `metadata()` (engine/src/handlers/helpers/programs/helpers.ts:174) feeds `reviewMetadata` straight into `standalonePackets` -> `selectStandaloneReviewers` (helpers.ts:248) and into `prepareFreshStandaloneReview` (standalone.ts:34-53), and no downstream guard catches the false positive for non-source paths — a scope of only `docker-compose.yml` (.yml is not in SOURCE_EXTENSIONS, so `sourceOrTestChanged` is false and the `docsOnly && sourceOrTestChanged` boundary check at core/standalone-review.ts:262 never fires) yields docsOnly=true, dropping silent-failure-hunter (line 293) and adding comment-analyzer (line 298); for `src/docker/build.ts` the same misclassification instead hard-aborts the run at that boundary check. The `every()` quantifier narrows how often it triggers but does not contain it."},{"finding_id":"standalone-review:silent-failure-hunter-1","verdict":"upheld","reasoning":"The discarded message does reach an operator-facing surface: the bare null flows to orchestration.ts:715-726 (\"registered orchestration program is malformed\"), :853-857 (same), :645-647 (\"restart currently requires a registered Wave Gate run\") and :1162-1164 (\"this registered program does not accept user decisions\"), so a wave-gate/remediation registration that failed only its input validation is reported with a generic or actively wrong reason; the null cannot be defended as dispatch signalling for an already-matched variant either, since parseRegisteredPanelProgram only accepts kinds architecture/refutation and can never claim a `kind: \"remediation\"` record."}]}